$NetBSD$

To let sshd accept the keys people publish on GitHub:

	AuthorizedKeysCommand ${PREFIX}/libexec/github-keys
	AuthorizedKeysCommandUser nobody

in /etc/ssh/sshd_config, then "/etc/rc.d/sshd reload".

Where a local account name is not the GitHub login, list the exceptions
in ${PKG_SYSCONFDIR}/github-keys.map, one "localname githublogin" pair
per line.  Accounts not listed keep their own name.

No credentials are sent, so only keys the user has chosen to publish are
visible -- and whoever controls that GitHub account controls the login.
Worth deciding on purpose before enabling it for privileged accounts.
